{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-28", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curve (35 mm, ILFORD ILFOTEC HC (1+31), 6.5 min, 20 C, intermittent agitation) and spectral sensitivity digitised from the Ilford data sheet (HP5 Plus technical information, April 2010, pages 1 and 5). Original data are property of Harman technology Limited (Ilford). The data sheet gives relative log exposure only: the exposure axis was anchored so that the speed point (density = fog + 0.1) lies at log10(0.8/ISO 400) lux-s, and shifted by -1.44 log lux-s so that 0 is the mid-grey exposure at box speed. Sensitivity offset chosen so that mid-grey renders at the reference level; sensitivity is the sheet's relative (linear) wedge-spectrogram curve under tungsten light, used as given. Tail above the sheet range extrapolated with decaying slope. Single development time (the sheet shows one curve). ", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format and wavelength grid taken from spektrafilm. grain_scale is an ESTIMATE (no data sheet value): target RMS granularity 14 assumed from the film class (similar to Kodak T-MAX / Tri-X class); simulated value at density 1.0 was 14.3 before scaling."}, "info": {"stock": "ilford_hp5_plus", "name": "Ilford HP5 Plus Black and White Negative Film, ILFOTEC HC", "type": "negative", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "strong", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "bw", "densitometer": "diffuse_visual", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "grain_scale": 0.978, "default_look": {"paper_grade": 3.0, "grain": 1.0, "print_ev": -0.4, "paper": "ilford_multigrade_iv_rc", "taking_filter": "gelb8", "taking_filter_amount": 0.3}, "card": {"maker": "Ilford", "iso": 400, "type": "Schwarzwei\u00dfnegativfilm", "rms": null, "additional": "Datenblatt (ohne Zahlenwerte)", "text": "Der vielseitige Allrounder: weiches, gut sichtbares Korn, gro\u00dfer Belichtungsspielraum, verzeiht Fehler. L\u00e4sst sich gut pushen (EI 800 bis 3200).", "source": "Ilford HP5 Plus", "process": "Schwarzwei\u00df-Negativentwicklung", "period": "HP5 Plus seit 1989; wird hergestellt", "suitable": ["Reportage und Stra\u00dfe", "Portr\u00e4t bei Tageslicht und Innenr\u00e4umen", "Pushen auf EI 800 bis 3200"], "less_suitable": ["feinste Vergr\u00f6\u00dferungen", "sehr glatte Haut"], "tips": ["Aufnahmefilter Gr\u00fcn (11): Der Look \u201eAbgestimmt\u201c legt ihn bereits mit etwa 50 % davor (Haut beh\u00e4lt Tiefe, Laub wird heller); \u201eKeiner\u201c oder \u201eDatenblatt\u201c zeigt die rohe Wiedergabe.", "Filmlooks \u201eHP5 \u00b7 Reportage\u201c (Papiergrad 3) und \u201eHP5 \u00b7 verblasst\u201c (Papiergrad 2, matt 2,5) zeigen zwei typische Looks."], "facts": [{"text": "Die HP-Reihe begann 1931 mit hypersensiblen Platten; HP5 erschien 1976 und HP5 Plus 1989, mit kubischem Korn. Der wichtigste Mitbewerber ist Kodak Tri-X 400.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilford_HP5_Plus"}, {"text": "Laut Datenblatt gibt HP5 Plus gute Ergebnisse von EI 400 bis EI 3200 mit verl\u00e4ngerter Entwicklung (DD-X, HC, Microphen, RT Rapid).", "source": "Ilford HP5 Plus, Technical Information"}]}, "grain_siz